<newsitem itemid="62635" id="root" date="1996-09-18" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Britannic H1 pretax operating profit steady.</title>
<headline>Britannic H1 pretax operating profit steady.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.20		   vs 9.27</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.0		    vs 4.6</p>
<p> Life, pension income   189.9		  vs 169.1</p>
<p> General pretax	   0.2 loss	     vs 1.7 profit</p>
<p> Pretax operating	 25.8		   vs 25.9</p>
<p> Group pre-tax profit   27.2		   vs 30.9</p>
<p> Investment return	1.45 loss	    vs 1.72 loss</p>
<p> Tax paid		   8.53		   vs 8.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  18.64		  vs 22.55</p>
<p>NOTE - Britannic Assurance Plc said that including the effect of realised and unrealised gains and losses on stockholder investments of 1.4 million stg, the group profit before tax on an EU accounts directive basis fell by 11.9 percent to 27.2 million stg from 30.9 million stg for the same period the year before. Earnings per share fell by 17.9 percent to 9.75 pence from 11.87 pence, it added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
